On the ultimate viewing, he paused on the package where Alexander was linking demonic possession with three decrepit old men singing a silly ditty and, quite frankly, making pork chops of themselves, while Eloise Shakti apparently presided over the whole unholy mess. Eloise 
\f2\i and 
\f1\i0 Sarah Jacobson, Midler noted, were on that platform\'97a fact the show drew no attention to. Clearly Alexander did not want to implicate his trophy wife in all the spell-casting. Another fact the broadcast side-stepped was the number of Elvi in the crowd\'97easily half by Midler\'92s estimates on the footage he\'92d seen.\
If the younger Shakti thought it was time to seize power and air his family grievances on live-broadcast TV, Midler could work with that. If he wanted to feed his dear mater to sharks, then okay, there were worse ways to die.\
\
The Elvi unsettled him. While Midler reviewed the broadcast, there was an Elvi band playing in the bar downstairs, and potentially thousands more roaming the village. Midler reassessed the tactical value of them clogging the streets and distracting the locals, and weighed them less as a buffer on his flanks and more of a mildly entertaining horde of Visigoths on his doorstep.\
Maybe they were nothing. Alexander\'92s portrayal of a mass mind-control was just a tacky music festival, though why Eloise Shakti wanted to attend was beyond his reckoning. Maybe the Elvi just got into everything these days, like possums in your roof.\
Major Midler hated fighting possums.\
He thumbed through intelligence reports from inside the compound; Shakti the younger had support of most of those with guns, but not total support. How various civilian factions leaned was less clear.\
What remained were his orders: neutralise Shakti and take the compound.\
With all the entertainment and other chaotic factors he could take  compound and get a two-for-one on the divided Shaktis as well.\
Midler reviewed the aerial view of Sublime Point. The auditorium was dark; the rest of the compound was not. Lamps still lit the internal roads, and the perimeter weapons had neither exploded nor thoughtfully turned themselves towards Eloise\'92s house.\
Midler looked out the clubhouse window to the eighteenth hole. Golfers were still playing in. He looked down at a demand from the club committee that he vacate function room and quit the golf course. He called for his adjutant, and retrieved his cigar from the rim of a saucer bearing the golf club\'92s crest.\
His adjutant appeared at the door. \'93Sir.\'94\
\'93Suspend Operation Herm\'e8s.\'94
